Subject: [PATCH] feat: binance_reconcile_fetch -- shared read-only Binance
 reconcile-source fetcher (v0.13.0) (#5)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Task 3 L3.  ed-seykota and mexc-4h-momentum each carry a near-byte-identical
read-only Binance USDⓈ-M reconcile-source fetcher (balance / positionRisk /
userTrades / openOrders / openAlgoOrders -> reconcile-source/v1).  Extract the
shared core to a single authoritative module.

src/trade_alerts/binance_reconcile_fetch.py (new, pure):
  * does NOT import binance_trading_toolkit -- the caller builds the client
    (toolkit BinanceFuturesClient or any object with the same read surface)
    and passes it in; credential resolution / mainnet detection / EXCHANGE
    dispatch stay in each repo's credential layer.
  * BinanceReconcileParams injects per-repo differences: query_symbols
    (Binance-native, userTrades is per-symbol), scope_symbol (None = every
    symbol for momentum, the symbol string for seykota), doc_symbol,
    to_ledger_symbol (identity vs momentum_ledger_symbol GPSUSDT->GPS_USDT),
    lookback_hours.
  * fetch() always emits symbols_queried + fills_possibly_truncated (a
    harmless superset for the single-symbol consumer; exchange_ledger_compare
    ignores unknown keys).
  * _order_rows carries the T1-6 PR #41 algo field fix (orderType /
    createTime) -- seykota gains it too.
  * run() reuses ledger_reconcile.atomic_write; never raises.

Pure addition -- no existing module or behavior changes.  Exports
BinanceReconcileParams + momentum_ledger_symbol from the package;
fetch/run stay on the submodule (matches the ledger_reconcile import style).
tests/test_binance_reconcile_fetch.py: 16 tests (fake client).  Suite 94 -> 110.
pyproject + __init__.__version__ -> 0.13.0; release runbook note + consumer table.

